INT. DEFUNCT PLANETARIUM - NIGHT

Domed ceiling, cracked and starless. Rows of reclined seats like a ribcage. A projector the size of a car squats in the centre, wrapped in cables.

RUTH ALMEIDA (30s, black parka, cropped hair, a face that gives nothing) stands on the dais with a duffel. Her eyes go to every exit. Four doors. Two chained.

A man in the dark. Tall. Brown overcoat. Holds a phone out in front of him like a torch. This is the STRANGER (50s).

STRANGER
You're early.

RUTH
You're late.

STRANGER
I'm exactly on time. I've been here since noon.

RUTH
Then you know the doors.

STRANGER
I know the doors.

He crosses the aisle. His shoes tick on dead tile. Ruth sets the duffel on the projector base and unzips it two inches. Cash. Rubber-banded. A glint of a second thing underneath.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
That's not what we agreed.

RUTH
It's what I brought.

A DOOR slams somewhere above. Both look up. Footsteps on the catwalk. Then a high, bright voice from the dark.

DANIEL (O.S.)
Ruth? Ruth, it's me!

RUTH
(to the Stranger, flat)
You brought someone.

STRANGER
I didn't.

RUTH
Someone followed you.

DANIEL (O.S.)
Don't shoot. I'm coming down.

DANIEL OKAFOR (20s, soaked jacket, hands high, a courier's badge on a lanyard) clatters down the aisle steps, eyes wide, breath ragged. He stops five feet from the dais. He's looking at the Stranger.

DANIEL
You told me he'd be alone.

RUTH
He is.

DANIEL
He has a gun.

STRANGER
Everyone here has a gun, son.

Ruth steps between them with her hand inside her parka, her gaze on the Stranger, her shoulder angled toward Daniel. The Stranger lowers the phone, lets its light sweep the floor, and lets his own hand rest at his belt. Daniel edges backward until his heel catches a seat arm, and the seat clunks, and all three of them flinch at the sound. The projector hums as if listening.

RUTH
Who are you?

STRANGER
You don't need that.

RUTH
Names are what I need.

STRANGER
Then call me what you like.

RUTH
I'll call you what the file called you.

STRANGER
(a pause)
Marcus Hale. Retired.

RUTH
Nobody's retired.

MARCUS
Fair.

He says it like a man putting down a coin.

On the catwalk, another DOOR. A flashlight beam sweeps the dome. Rows of seats leap out of the dark one by one. Daniel drops behind the nearest row. Ruth doesn't move. Marcus smiles very slightly.

MARCUS (CONT'D)
That one is mine.

RUTH
You said you came alone.

MARCUS
I said I was alone. It's not the same.

The beam finds Ruth's face. Holds. Behind the light a figure steps out: TESSA QUINN (40s, long coat, flashlight in one hand, a pistol held low in the other), her expression as neutral as a closed door.

TESSA
Evening, Ruth.

RUTH
Detective.

TESSA
It's Tessa tonight.

RUTH
It's never Tessa.

Tessa descends two steps. Marcus slides sideways along the dais, hand away from his belt now. Daniel peeks over the seat back like a child watching a fight.

DANIEL
(whisper)
Ruth, I didn't call her.

RUTH
I know.

TESSA
Daniel didn't call me. Marcus did.

DANIEL
What?

Ruth looks at Marcus. Marcus looks at the ceiling, at the cracked painted stars, as if the answer might be written there.

MARCUS
I've got a pension, Ruth.

RUTH
You said retired.

MARCUS
I said a lot of things.

The projector hums louder. A dull bulb in its belly blinks on, throws a wavering white ellipse onto the dome, and suddenly the whole ceiling is a pale moon with four small shadows moving under it.

TESSA
Everybody put your hands where I can see them.

Nobody does. Ruth's hand comes out of her parka. Empty. She lifts the duffel and holds it out over the edge of the dais as if offering it to a guest.

RUTH
Take it, Detective.

TESSA
Put it down.

RUTH
You wanted the bag. Here's the bag.

She lets it go. It hits the floor. The zip splits. Bundles spill, and with them a flat black device the size of a deck of cards, its red light blinking.

Tessa looks at it. Marcus looks at it. Daniel looks at all of them.

DANIEL
What is that?

A voice crackles from the catwalk, thin and metallic.

SERGEANT BRANDT (O.S.)
Quinn, bomb squad says do not touch it!

Nobody answers. The red light blinks faster.
